<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-17">17 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">H. L. Hunley sinks USS Housatonic</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Confederate submarine rammed a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/torpedo">torpedo</a> into the Union warship off Charleston, the first sinking of an enemy ship by a submarine. The Hunley was lost with all eight crew that night.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-20">20 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Union army suffers heavy losses at the Battle of Olustee</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At the Battle of Olustee, or Ocean Pond, in Baker County near Lake City, the Union army suffered a casualty rate of one in three. It was the largest battle fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mississippi-river.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-12">12 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Confederate troops massacre surrendering Union soldiers at Fort Pillow</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At Fort Pillow on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi River</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a>, Confederate soldiers under Nathan Bedford Forrest massacred Union soldiers trying to surrender, killing most of the African American soldiers who surrendered. It is also called the Fort Pillow Massacre.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/confederate-states-of-america">Confederate States of America</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi River</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-17">17 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Confederate forces attack Plymouth, North Carolina</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Confederate forces attacked Plymouth, North Carolina, opening the Battle of Plymouth in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a>. The fighting went on until 20 April, in the city and across the surrounding Washington County.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/confederate-states-of-america">Confederate States of America</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-22">22 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Coinage Act puts 'In God We Trust' on US coins</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Congress authorised a new two-cent coin, the first to bear the motto 'In God We Trust'. It spread to other coins and became the official US national motto in 1956.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-30">30 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Kirby Smith's Confederates attack Union troops at Jenkins' Ferry</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Kirby Smith's Confederates attacked federal troops retreating across the Saline River at Jenkins' Ferry, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arkansas">Arkansas</a>. A tactical Union victory, it was seen by the Confederacy as a strategic success: it kept Frederick Steele from holding southwest Arkansas.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/confederate-states-of-america">Confederate States of America</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-9">9 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Sniper kills Union general John Sedgwick at Spotsylvania</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Moments after telling his men that Confederate sharpshooters 'couldn't hit an elephant at this distance', General Sedgwick was shot dead. He was the highest-ranking Union officer killed in the war.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-26">26 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Lincoln signs the act creating the Montana Territory</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln">Abraham Lincoln</a> signed the law organising the Territory of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montana">Montana</a>, an organised incorporated territory of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. It lasted until 8 November 1889, when it was admitted to the Union as the 41st state.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln">Abraham Lincoln</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montana">Montana</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/robert-e-lee" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-e-lee.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-31">31 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Grant's and Lee's armies meet in the Battle of Cold Harbor</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Mechanicsville, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-e-lee">Robert E. Lee</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/army-of-northern-virginia">Army of Northern Virginia</a> met the Army of the Potomac, directed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulysses-s-grant">Ulysses S. Grant</a>. Thousands of Union soldiers were killed or wounded in the frontal assault of 3 June.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-e-lee">Robert E. Lee</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/army-of-northern-virginia">Army of Northern Virginia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulysses-s-grant">Ulysses S. Grant</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/ulysses-s-grant" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ulysses-s-grant.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-12">12 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Grant withdraws from Cold Harbor and moves his army south</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulysses-s-grant">Ulysses S. Grant</a> pulled his Union troops from their position at Cold Harbor, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, and moved south, leaving the battle to the Confederate army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-e-lee">Robert E. Lee</a>. Thousands of Union soldiers had been killed or wounded in the frontal assault of 3 June.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulysses-s-grant">Ulysses S. Grant</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-e-lee">Robert E. Lee</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-21">21 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of Jerusalem Plank Road begins near Petersburg</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Two Union infantry corps tried to sever the Weldon Railroad near Petersburg, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, but were attacked and driven off by the Confederate Third Corps, chiefly the division of William Mahone. The Union then began extending its siege lines west.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/confederate-states-of-america">Confederate States of America</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/william-tecumseh-sherman" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-tecumseh-sherman.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-27">27 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Johnston's Confederates repulse Sherman at Kennesaw Mountain</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Union Major General William T. Sherman launched his most significant frontal assault of the Atlanta campaign against Joseph E. Johnston's Army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>. It failed, but the Confederate win did not halt Sherman's advance on Atlanta.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/confederate-states-of-america">Confederate States of America</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-tecumseh-sherman">William T. Sherman</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/choshu-domain" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/choshu-domain.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-8">8 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Shinsengumi attack shishi plotters at the Ikedaya Inn</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shinsengumi">Shinsengumi</a>, the Bakufu's special police force, fought an armed encounter with shishi, among them masterless <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samurai">samurai</a> of the Chōshū, Tosa and Higo domains, at the Ikedaya Inn. The incident brought the Shinsengumi considerable fame.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa Shogunate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shinsengumi">Shinsengumi</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/choshu-domain">Chōshū</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-22">22 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Hood attacks Sherman in the Battle of Atlanta</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Confederate General John Bell Hood struck Sherman's armies east of Atlanta, killing Union General James McPherson. The attack failed, and Atlanta's fall in September boosted Lincoln's re-election.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-24">24 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Jubal Early drives Crook's Union army from the Shenandoah Valley</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At the Second Battle of Kernstown, the Confederate Army of the Valley under Jubal Early defeated George Crook's Union army and drove it from the Shenandoah Valley over the Potomac. Early then launched the Confederacy's last major raid into Union territory.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/confederate-states-of-america">Confederate States of America</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-18">18 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Union troops strike the Weldon Railroad at Globe Tavern</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">South of Petersburg, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, a Union force under Gouverneur K. Warren destroyed miles of the Weldon Railroad and withstood strong Confederate attacks. It was the first Union victory of the Richmond–Petersburg Campaign.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-22">22 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The first Geneva Convention is signed</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Twelve states signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a> Convention protecting wounded soldiers and the medical staff caring for them. It grew out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-dunant">Henry Dunant</a>'s campaign and founded modern humanitarian law.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-1">1 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Confederates evacuate Atlanta</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">General John Bell Hood abandoned Atlanta, blowing up ammunition trains as he left, and Sherman's troops entered the next day. The capture of the rail hub revived Lincoln's re-election hopes.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/william-tecumseh-sherman" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-tecumseh-sherman.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-18">18 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">John Bell Hood opens the Franklin–Nashville campaign</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Confederate general John Bell Hood began a series of battles in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alabama">Alabama</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a> and northwestern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, also known as Hood's Tennessee campaign. It failed in its aim of drawing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-tecumseh-sherman">William Tecumseh Sherman</a> back out of Georgia and lasted until 27 December.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/confederate-states-of-america">Confederate States of America</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-tecumseh-sherman">William Tecumseh Sherman</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/winchester" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/winchester.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-19">19 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Sheridan defeats Jubal Early at the Third Battle of Winchester</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winchester">Winchester</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, Union Major General Philip Sheridan defeated Lieutenant General Jubal Early in one of the largest and bloodiest battles in the Shenandoah Valley. The Union counted some 5,000 casualties, the Confederates about 4,000 of 15,500.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winchester">Winchester</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-2">2 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Confederates repulse a Union attack at Saltville, Virginia</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Confederate forces defeated a Union attack near the town of Saltville, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, in the First Battle of Saltville. A massacre of wounded Union prisoners followed, and the battle is also known as the Saltville Massacre.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/confederate-states-of-america">Confederate States of America</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-15">15 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Confederates capture the Union garrison at Glasgow, Missouri</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">During Price's Missouri Expedition, the Union garrison of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glasgow">Glasgow</a>, Missouri, surrendered to Confederate forces. The capture gave them needed weapons and lifted Confederate morale, which had been dented by the defeat at the Battle of Pilot Knob.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/confederate-states-of-america">Confederate States of America</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-19">19 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Sheridan rallies to defeat Early at the Battle of Cedar Creek</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Jubal Early's Confederates took over 1,000 prisoners and 20 guns in a morning attack in the Shenandoah Valley, but Philip Sheridan's Union army rallied in the afternoon and drove them away. The battle ended the last Confederate threat to Washington.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-23">23 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Union forces defeat Sterling Price at the Battle of Westport</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kansas">Kansas</a> City, Missouri, Union troops under Samuel R. Curtis decisively defeated the outnumbered Confederates of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pound-sterling">Sterling</a> Price, with more than 30,000 men engaged. It ended the last major Confederate offensive west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi River</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-25">25 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Union troops defeat Sterling Price's Confederates at Marais des Cygnes</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After their defeat at Westport on 23 October, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pound-sterling">Sterling</a> Price's Confederate raiders withdrew into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kansas">Kansas</a>; Union troops then defeated them at Marais des Cygnes in Linn County, at Mine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a> and at the Marmiton River.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-27">27 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Benjamin Butler's Union attack at Fair Oaks and Darbytown Road fails</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Union General Benjamin Butler attacked in Henrico County, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, as part of the Richmond–Petersburg campaign of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a>. The Battle of Fair Oaks &amp; Darbytown Road was fought over two days, and by the next day he had been repulsed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-31">31 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Nevada becomes the 36th US state</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nevada">Nevada</a> was admitted to the Union during the Civil War, with Republicans keen on its votes for Lincoln's re-election and support for the 13th Amendment. It is still called the 'Battle Born State'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-4">4 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Forrest's cavalry strike the Union supply base at Johnsonville</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Ending a 23-day raid through western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a>, Confederate cavalry under Nathan Bedford Forrest destroyed 28 Union boats and barges and millions of dollars of supplies at Johnsonville. It hampered George H. Thomas's plans against Hood's invasion of Tennessee.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/confederate-states-of-america">Confederate States of America</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-13">13 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Breckinridge's Confederates rout Union troops at Bull's Gap</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The three-day Battle of Bull's Gap in Hamblen and Greene counties, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a>, ended in a Union rout, as Confederates under Major General John C. Breckinridge pursued them to Strawberry Plains. Breckinridge had been vice president from 1857 to 1861.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/confederate-states-of-america">Confederate States of America</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/savannah" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/savannah.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-15">15 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Sherman leaves Atlanta on his March to the Sea</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After burning much of Atlanta, William T. Sherman's army set off for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savannah">Savannah</a>. Its destruction of railways, crops and property across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> aimed to break the Confederacy's capacity and will to fight.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savannah">Savannah</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-29">29 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Colorado troops massacre Cheyenne and Arapaho at Sand Creek</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Colonel John Chivington's volunteer cavalry attacked a peaceful camp at Sand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colorado">Colorado</a>, killing about 150 to 200 people, mostly women, children and the elderly. Congressional inquiries condemned the attack.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-30">30 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Hood's Army of Tennessee suffers heavy losses at Franklin</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">John Bell Hood's Confederate Army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a> made repeated frontal assaults on Union forces under John Schofield at Franklin, Tennessee, but could not stop their planned withdrawal to Nashville. It was one of the worst Confederate disasters of the war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/confederate-states-of-america">Confederate States of America</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/william-tecumseh-sherman" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-tecumseh-sherman.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-13">13 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Union troops under Hazen seize Fort McAllister near Savannah</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Union forces under William B. Hazen overwhelmed the small Confederate force holding Fort McAllister, on the Ogeechee River near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savannah">Savannah</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, late in Sherman's March to the Sea. Its fall allowed Sherman to capture Savannah.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-tecumseh-sherman">Sherman</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savannah">Savannah</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/second-schleswig-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-schleswig-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">War</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/second-schleswig-war">Second Schleswig War</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Second Schleswig War was fought in 1864 between Denmark and the allied German powers Prussia and Austria.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dybbol" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-dybbol.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dybbol">Battle of Dybbøl</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Dybbøl was the decisive engagement of the Second Schleswig War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/charlottetown-conference" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charlottetown-conference.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/charlottetown-conference">Charlottetown Conference</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Charlottetown Conference was a meeting of delegates from the Province of Canada, Nova Scotia, New Brunswick and Prince Edward Island, held at Charlottetown in September 1864.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/tengu-party-rebellion" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tengu-party-rebellion.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/tengu-party-rebellion">Tengu Party Rebellion</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Tengu Party Rebellion was a rising of radical loyalist samurai of the Mito domain in 1864, during the last years of the Tokugawa shogunate.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-orakau" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-orakau.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-orakau">Battle of Ōrākau</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Ōrākau was fought from 31 March to 2 April 1864 in the Waikato, New Zealand, the last major battle of the British invasion of the Waikato.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/long-walk-of-the-navajo">Long Walk of the Navajo</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Long Walk of the Navajo was the forced removal of the Navajo people by the US Army in 1864 from their homeland in present-day Arizona and New Mexico to the Bosque Redondo reservation.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-vienna-1864">Treaty of Vienna (1864)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Vienna was signed on 30 October 1864 between Denmark and the victors of the Second Schleswig War, Prussia and Austria.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/russian-judicial-reform-of-1864">Russian judicial reform of 1864</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Russian judicial reform of 1864 was one of the Great Reforms of Tsar Alexander II, which reorganised the courts of the Russian Empire.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">War</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/tsilhqotin-war">Tsilhqot'in War</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Tsilhqot'in War was a conflict in 1864 between the Tsilhqot'in people of the Chilcotin plateau and the colony of British Columbia.</p></div></li></ol></section>
